ork, NY", "dates": "July 2026 \u2013 Present", "commitment": "Part Time", "subtitle": "Principal Business Strategist \u2013 GTM Plan, Business Architectural Roadmap, Blueprint to Obtain Necessary Funding \u2013 Healthcare FinTech Start-Up", "bullets": ["Own go-to-market for an AI compliance product sold into independent clinical practices \u2014 segmentation, positioning, pricing tiers ($99/$249), channel strategy, and the sequencing that determines which motion gets funded first.", "Designed and launched a 30\u201340 interview customer discovery sprint to size real addressable demand \u2014 screener, interview guide, scoring rubric, and 150-practice candidate universe built from scratch \u2014 classifying prospects by platform dependence against a pre-agreed threshold that fires a documented kill/pivot decision instead of a debate.", "Concluded that distribution \u2014 not product \u2014 decides the outcome, redirecting GTM toward malpractice-carrier and professional-association channel partnerships after modeling that a direct human sales motion cannot carry a 12\u201318 month CAC payback at those price points.", "Set the unit-economic gates the motion is now measured against: blended CAC under $900, payback under 12 months, monthly churn under 5%, time-to-first-value under 7 days.", "Mapped a $0.76B category projected to reach $5.9B by 2035 (22.8% CAGR), benchmarked five direct comparables across four structural models, and built a decision tree of four exit paths with base-rate odds attached \u2014 including the cautionary comparable that won regulatory clearance and still failed on commercialization.", "Produced the customer- and investor-facing collateral the company now sells with: pitch deck, competitive battlecards, partner negotiation sheets, and an eight-document executive round table with per-presentation talking points.", "Ran financial forecasting (P&L, tool-stack cost model, Year-1 ARR band) and barriers-to-entry analysis to price strategic alternatives before capital committed; recommended a ~$2.15M non-dilutive federal funding route over an equity raise, tied to a dated decision gate.", "Applied scenario planning and second- and third-order consequence analysis across business, technology, regulatory, and organizational exposure \u2014 surfacing downstream consequences before commitments locked in.", "Built the multi-tenant, role-scoped client engagement tracker that runs the advisory practice using Claude Code \u2014 including 60 automated tests asserting cross-client data isolation \u2014 with no prior engineering background."], "bullet_ids": [116, 121, 120, 117, 115, 122, 124, 125, 123], "achievement_ids": ["lim-gtm-ownership", "lim-customer-discovery-sprint", "lim-distribution-pivot", "lim-unit-economic-gates", "lim-market-sizing-exit-paths", "lim-collateral", "lim-non-dilutive-capital", "lim-scenario-planning", "lim-claude-code-tracker"], "claim_ids": [["ach:lim-gtm-ownership", "metric:lim-gtm-ownership:pricing-tiers"], ["ach:lim-customer-discovery-sprint", "metric:lim-customer-discovery-sprint:interviews", "metric:lim-customer-discovery-sprint:account-universe"], ["ach:lim-distribution-pivot", "metric:lim-distribution-pivot:cac-payback-modeled"], ["ach:lim-unit-economic-gates", "metric:lim-unit-economic-gates:blended-cac-cap", "metric:lim-unit-economic-gates:payback-cap", "metric:lim-unit-economic-gates:monthly-churn-cap", "metric:lim-unit-economic-gates:ttfv-cap"], ["ach:lim-market-sizing-exit-paths", "metric:lim-market-sizing-exit-paths:category-size-2025", "metric:lim-market-sizing-exit-paths:category-size-2035", "metric:lim-market-sizing-exit-paths:cagr"], ["ach:lim-collateral", "metric:lim-collateral:round-table-documents"], ["ach:lim-non-dilutive-capital", "metric:lim-non-dilutive-capital:non-dilutive-route"], ["ach:lim-scenario-planning"], ["ach:lim-claude-code-tracker", "metric:lim-claude-code-tracker:automated-tests"]]}], "core_competencies": [{"label": "Go-To-Market & Revenue", "items": ["GTM s